I see a dark green vegetable on the cart.
That vegetable is not smooth.
It is a little strange.
I do not know that vegetable.
I ask the vendor.
"What is this?" I ask.
"This is 'karela'," he says.
"Do you want this?" he asks.
"How is its taste?" I ask.
"Its taste is bitter," he says.
Bitter!
I do not like a bitter taste.
"Today I do not want karela," I say.
He smiles.
I only buy the tomatoes and spinach.
I give rupees.
I do not take that bitter vegetable.
